WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.443 --> 00:00:03.026
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.970
[Joe] Hey, Rob, this is Joe in Memphis.

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.880
I have a sports question for you.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:14.020
Do you agree with me that
Tom Brady is a lizard person?

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:17.100
I think there's some compelling evidence.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.340
I mostly go back to,
well, among other things,

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:23.210
he doesn't age like a normal human being.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.580
He's won an inordinate
amount of Super Bowl rings,

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:29.050
but my bigger thing is
the clues given to us

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:30.053
by Bill Belichick.

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:34.240
Bill Belichick, I believe
is actually a hero

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:35.320
for our society.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.300
He, I think in his own way

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.500
is trying to signal us

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:42.740
that Tom Brady is a lizard person.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:46.530
He's never, Bill Belichick
never looks happy.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:48.670
Even given all of the success he's had,

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:51.210
he always looks like a grouch.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:53.639
I think if we were to watch
any of his press conferences

00:00:53.639 --> 00:00:56.677
he would probably be
blinking in Morse code,

00:00:56.677 --> 00:00:58.040
"Watch out for Tom Brady.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:00:59.090
He's a lizard person."

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:01.090
So I want to know where you fall

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:03.710
and if so, if he is a lizard person,

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:05.610
should the Patriots and Tampa Bay

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:08.020
be stripped of all their
Super Bowl trophies?

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:08.853
Thanks again,

00:01:08.853 --> 00:01:10.430
and I'll take my answer off the air.

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:11.263
Yeah, thanks, Joe.

00:01:11.263 --> 00:01:12.830
I've given a lot of thought to this.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:16.633
Look, as lizard people go,

00:01:18.056 --> 00:01:23.056
I think it's, he ticks
all the boxes, Brady.

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:30.380
As you say, he does not age,

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:31.700
he's a freak of nature.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:34.040
It's very clear that Bill Belichick

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.950
has been giving press conferences

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:39.053
like prisoner of war videos for years.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:42.760
In fact, I always wanted
to do my interviews

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:43.930
like Bill Belichick,

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:46.497
and I would have loved
to have asked Belichick,

00:01:46.497 --> 00:01:47.810
"Is Brady a lizard person?"

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:49.440
'Cause it would have been,

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:50.750
could be, I don't know.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:53.523
And just thinking about
Kansas City next weekend.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:59.360
I do like that Brady is in
the pretty boy hall of fame.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.530
That's more important than being for me,

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:02.940
a lizard person,

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.960
is that he's a very pretty man.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:09.560
And I have a very soft spot in my heart

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:10.900
for pretty men.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:13.313
And I love to see him do well.

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:15.993
And if he is a lizard person,

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:22.860
it's made up for by the fact

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:26.063
that he is more importantly,
extraordinarily pretty.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:27.733
Thanks, Joe.

00:02:27.733 --> 00:02:29.117
That was a good question.

